title: "rfurze.co.uk — multiscale methods for lubrication"
message: >-
  If you use this material, please cite it using the following metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Robin
    family-names: Furze
    email: py07rf@leeds.ac.uk
    affiliation: University of Leeds
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6692-4982'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/RFurze/Home'
url: 'https://rfurze.co.uk'
abstract: >-
  Website and runnable notebooks demonstrating the numerical methods behind
  multiscale computational tribology — the Heterogeneous Multiscale Method
  (HMM), microscale cell problems, and macro/micro coupling for friction and
  lubrication in artificial hip-joint bearings.
keywords:
  - Heterogeneous Multiscale Method
  - multiscale modelling
  - tribology
  - elastohydrodynamic lubrication
  - Reynolds equation
  - homogenisation
